__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Never commit a machine-specific path. The declared paths live in the repository's path config; an
# override belongs in the environment, not in the tree, or the tree stops being cloneable elsewhere.
.env
*.local.json

# Generated by the pipeline. These are outputs, never sources; the guard in scripts/check_object_drift.py
# is about retired objects and does not cover them.
measurement/out/
*.items.jsonl
*.trial.jsonl

# paper2agent conversion scratch (working dirs, not deliverables)
.p2a-work/

# Source papers. They are INPUTS that live outside this repository's scope and are 1-10 MB each; a
# clone should not carry them. Nothing in the pipeline reads them from here - the reference library
# keeps its own extracted text under the skill directories.
*.pdf
# The Stage 2 figure PDF is a DELIVERABLE, not a build by-product: it carries the captions and is one of
# the four formats the manuscript needs, so it is tracked even though PDFs generally are not.
!viz/figures_stage2.pdf
!viz/manuscript.pdf
!viz/supplementary_information.pdf

# A re-downloadable raw corpus. The DERIVED labels beside it are committed because they are not
# reproducible without GPU time (modeA_items.jsonl holds the rater's per-item answers); the raw jfleg
# dump is one `load_dataset` call away and is excluded on that basis alone.
measurement/o1_validation/jfleg_raw.jsonl

# The KaTeX distribution is third-party, copied in by the build and never hand-edited. It stopped being
# referenced when the mathematics renderer was unified on MathJax, so it stays out of the index.
viz/katex/
#
# MATHAJX IS A RUNTIME DEPENDENCY OF A TRACKED DELIVERABLE, NOT BUILD INPUT. An HTML whose `mathjax/`
# directory is absent renders NO mathematics: the page opens, the TeX shows as raw `$...$`, and nothing
# errors. What a reader's browser actually fetches is tracked - the loader and the CHTML font set that
# `@font-face` pulls in - and the remaining ~24 MB of the distribution (SVG output, source maps, further
# font sets) is not, because no document references it.
viz/mathjax/*
!viz/mathjax/tex-mml-chtml.js
!viz/mathjax/output/
viz/mathjax/output/*
!viz/mathjax/output/chtml/
viz/mathjax/output/chtml/*
!viz/mathjax/output/chtml/fonts/
viz/mathjax/output/chtml/fonts/*
!viz/mathjax/output/chtml/fonts/woff-v2/
#
# viz/manuscript.html IS A DELIVERABLE AND IS TRACKED. It was ignored on the grounds that it is generated
# and can be rebuilt - true of what the OLD builder produced, which was a render of the PROTOCOL, and no
# longer true once the manuscript got its own builder. Its sibling `supplementary_information.html` was
# tracked the whole time, so the repository carried one deliverable and silently omitted the other, and a
# clone could not read the paper. A rule that outlives its subject does not announce itself.
# NOTE: viz/protocol.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the byte-for-byte copy the build
# read, and it is the recovery source - an entire section was once deleted by a bad edit and
# restored from it. A backup excluded from version control is not a backup.

# Scratch output from the figure QC run. It is generated, not authored.
viz/figures/_qc_tmp/

# Machine-local interpreter pointer for the pre-commit gate. Never committed: the repository
# must stay portable and no absolute path belongs in it.
.guard-python

# Node dependencies. MathJax is installed here and copied into the output directory at build
# time so the rendered documents need no network; the 121 MB install itself never enters history.
node_modules/

# transient: the OMML harvest page is regenerated by build_si_docx.py --harvest
viz/_mml_harvest.html
viz/_mml_map.json
# harvest page and MathML map are per-document now, derived from the output name
viz/*_mml_harvest.html
# TRACKED, though it looks like a build intermediate: it is the PROVENANCE of a tracked DOCX. The map
# records which MathML each source expression became, and the DOCX carries those equations as native OMML.
# Excluded, a clone holds a document whose equations cannot be traced to a source expression, cannot be
# rebuilt, and - since the coverage check reads this file - would report that the build has no mathematics to
# place. That is the same defect as `viz/manuscript.html` and `viz/mathjax/` above: a rule that outlived its
# subject, and the subject is now "an artefact a tracked deliverable depends on". The harvest PAGE stays
# ignored: it is regenerable in seconds and carries nothing the map does not.

# a downloaded installer that landed in the working tree; not project content, and an
# untracked binary swept in by `git add -A` is exactly how a repository grows 100 MB of accident
Hermes-Setup.exe
*Setup.exe
